---
import BlockLayout from '../../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';
import { reviewsBySlug } from '../../data/reviews';

const review = reviewsBySlug.get('openprinter')!;

const reviewJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Review',
  '@id': 'https://pointcast.xyz/reviews/openprinter#review',
  url: 'https://pointcast.xyz/reviews/openprinter',
  name: review.title,
  headline: review.title,
  description: review.dek,
  datePublished: '2026-09-21',
  inLanguage: 'en-US',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PointCast Review Lab', url: 'https://pointcast.xyz' },
  itemReviewed: {
    '@type': 'Product',
    name: 'Openprinter',
    brand: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Open Tools', url: 'https://www.opentools.studio/' },
    url: 'https://www.crowdsupply.com/open-tools/open-printer',
    category: 'Inkjet printer',
  },
  reviewRating: { '@type': 'Rating', ratingValue: review.rating, bestRating: 5, worstRating: 1 },
};

const photos = [
  { src: '/images/openprinter/on-wall.jpg', w: 1000, h: 1500, alt: 'Openprinter mounted on a white column with a roll on top and a printed chart hanging in a wire tray below', cap: 'The wall kit. Roll on top, tray below.' },
  { src: '/images/openprinter/on-desk.jpg', w: 1000, h: 1500, alt: 'Openprinter on a desk beside a laptop, printing from a paper roll', cap: 'On a desk it is a long grey bar.' },
  { src: '/images/openprinter/remove-roll.jpg', w: 1024, h: 765, alt: 'Hands lifting the paper roll off the top of the Openprinter to load sheets', cap: 'Lift the roll off to feed A4, A3, Letter or Tabloid sheets.' },
  { src: '/images/openprinter/cartridges.jpg', w: 1024, h: 576, alt: 'A black and a tri-color HP cartridge seated side by side in the Openprinter carriage', cap: 'HP 63 / 302 cartridges. Black alone, color alone, or both.' },
];
---

<BlockLayout legacy title={review.title} description={review.dek} image={review.image}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(reviewJsonLd)} />

  <article class="opr">
    <nav class="opr__bar" aria-label="Review navigation">
      <a href="/">POINTCAST</a>
      <a href="/reviews">REVIEWS</a>
      <span>SEPTEMBER 2026 · PUBLIC-SPEC</span>
      <a href="/reviews/openprinter.json">JSON ↗</a>
    </nav>

    <header class="opr__hero">
      <div class="opr__cover">
        <img src={review.image} width={review.imageWidth} height={review.imageHeight} alt={review.imageAlt} loading="eager" />
        <span class="opr__stamp">PRE-<br />LAUNCH</span>
      </div>
      <div class="opr__headline">
        <p class="opr__eyebrow">OPEN HARDWARE / INKJET / PARIS / CROWD SUPPLY, AUTUMN 2026</p>
        <h1>THE PRINTER<br />YOU <em>OWN</em></h1>
        <p>{review.dek}</p>
        <div class="opr__buttons">
          <a class="opr__button opr__button--ink" href="https://www.crowdsupply.com/open-tools/open-printer" rel="noopener">FOLLOW THE CAMPAIGN ↗</a>
          <a class="opr__button" href="https://www.opentools.studio/" rel="noopener">OPENTOOLS.STUDIO ↗</a>
          <a class="opr__button" href="#verdict">SKIP TO VERDICT ↓</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="opr__score"><strong>{review.rating}</strong><span>OUT OF 5 · PROVISIONAL</span></div>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="opr__lede">
        <p class="opr__drop"><span>E</span>very printer sold in the last twenty years was designed to be replaced. Openprinter is designed to be kept. A Raspberry Pi Zero W runs the open-source print server CUPS, an STM32 drives the cartridge, the plastics are 3D-printable, the frame is folded sheet metal, and the cartridges are the cheap HP ones you can already buy at a pharmacy. It prints from Windows, Mac, Linux, iPhone and Android with no driver from anyone.</p>
        <p>Two things separate it from every other inkjet. It takes a paper roll, 11 inches or 297 mm wide, up to 37.5 meters long, and cuts it to any length. And it prints with one cartridge, so an empty yellow never stops a black page. We reviewed the public spec, the site, and both Crowd Supply updates. No unit is in hand. Price and speed are still unannounced.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="opr__facts" aria-label="Openprinter facts">
        <div><strong>600</strong><span>DPI BLACK · 1200 COLOR</span></div>
        <div><strong>37.5</strong><span>METER ROLL, INTEGRATED CUTTER</span></div>
        <div><strong>01</strong><span>CARTRIDGE IS ENOUGH</span></div>
        <div><strong>TBD</strong><span>PRICE · PAGES PER MINUTE</span></div>
      </section>

      <section class="opr__chapter">
        <span class="opr__chapter-no">01</span>
        <div>
          <p class="opr__eyebrow">THE CASE</p>
          <h2>A ROLL CHANGES WHAT A PRINTER IS</h2>
          <p>Sheets are a habit. A roll with a cutter makes a receipt printer, a label maker, a banner press, a ticker and a zine machine out of the same grey bar. Open Tools shows to-do lists, a stock-sale flyer, a wall chart and a full contract page coming off the same spool. Lift the roll off its two arms and the slot takes A4, A3, Letter or Tabloid sheets. The whole thing is 50 by 10 by 11 centimeters without the roll, and a wall kit hangs it on a post with a wire tray underneath so the desk stays clear.</p>
          <p>The cartridge choice is the quiet engineering win. The HP 63, 302 and 803 family puts the printhead inside the cartridge. When a head clogs, and inkjet heads always clog, you replace a fifteen-dollar part instead of the machine. There is no chip handshake to refuse a refill, and Open Tools will sell 100 ml bottles and a refill kit. A control board with two seats, marked BLACK and COLOR, lets either sit alone.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="opr__grid" aria-label="Photographs from Open Tools">
        {photos.map((p) => (
          <figure>
            <img src={p.src} width={p.w} height={p.h} alt={p.alt} loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>{p.cap}</figcaption>
          </figure>
        ))}
      </section>

      <section class="opr__chapter opr__chapter--dark">
        <span class="opr__chapter-no">02</span>
        <div>
          <p class="opr__eyebrow">THE DOUBT</p>
          <h2>"OPEN" IS DOING SOME WORK</h2>
          <p>The files are promised under Creative Commons BY-NC-SA 4.0. That is a generous license for a hardware project, but it is not open source by the OSI definition, and the non-commercial clause means nobody else may sell a part, a kit or a fork. Open Tools has also filed a patent and a design registration. And the files ship only after the "final version," to avoid inconsistent copies in the wild. All of that is defensible. None of it is open today. What exists today is a promise of openness from a team that has so far kept its promises.</p>
          <p>The spec sheet has one wobble. The site lists Wi-Fi 802.11ac on a Pi Zero W, a board that only does b/g/n. Ethernet was on the June roadmap and is absent from the September spec. Speed has read "to be defined" all year. And the whole design rests on HP continuing to make one cartridge family. Integrated heads survive a handful of refills, not an infinite number. None of these are reasons to walk away. They are the questions we would ask before paying.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="opr__quote">
        <p>"NO PROPRIETARY DRIVERS, NO CARTRIDGE DRM, DESIGNED TO NEVER BECOME OBSOLETE."</p>
        <span>— OPEN TOOLS, CROWD SUPPLY PROJECT PAGE</span>
      </section>

      <section class="opr__split">
        <div>
          <p class="opr__eyebrow">THE PROOF</p>
          <h2>A REAL PROTOTYPE, NOT A RENDER</h2>
          <p>The June update reports black and full-color printing, sheet and roll handling, and a working cutter, with ink drying, nozzle cleaning cycles, dithering and design-for-manufacture still on the list. The September update says beta testers have units and the campaign opens this autumn with pricing. Bpifrance and SATT Lutech are backers, ENSCI is the design school behind it, and the printer is nominated for two French Design Awards. XDA, Hackster and Geeks Are Sexy have covered it. Three names are on the team page.</p>
          <p>Crowd Supply is the right venue. It holds funds, handles fulfillment, and has shipped a long line of open hardware. It also means this is a pre-order for a machine that does not yet exist in volume, from a first-time hardware team building an inkjet from scratch. Read the updates before you read the tiers.</p>
        </div>
        <aside>
          <span>SPEC KIT</span>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Brain</dt><dd>Raspberry Pi Zero W + STM32</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Server</dt><dd>CUPS, AirPrint</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Ink</dt><dd>HP 63 / 302 / 803, refillable</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Paper</dt><dd>A4, A3, Letter, Tabloid, 11 in roll</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Ports</dt><dd>USB-C, USB-A host, Wi-Fi, BT 4.1</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Screen</dt><dd>1.47 in TFT + jog wheel</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Power</dt><dd>24 V DC barrel</dd></div>
            <div><dt>License</dt><dd>CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, files after launch</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section class="opr__colors">
        <img src="/images/openprinter/colorways.jpg" width="2400" height="400" alt="Six Openprinter colorways in a row: classic grey, chalky blue, marble grey, clockwork orange, pistachio and terracotta" loading="lazy" />
        <p class="opr__eyebrow">SIX COLORWAYS · KIT OR ASSEMBLED · PRINT YOUR OWN SHELL IF YOU LIKE</p>
      </section>

      <section class="opr__chapter">
        <span class="opr__chapter-no">03</span>
        <div>
          <p class="opr__eyebrow">THE CHANGE</p>
          <h2>THE MISSING PERIPHERAL FOR A TOWN THAT PRINTS A WIRE</h2>
          <p>PointCast publishes numbered blocks to a wire. A machine on the wall that prints the wire onto paper, one block per morning, cut to length, is not a gadget for us. It is the peripheral we did not know we were waiting for. Mount it by the coffee pot. Feed it the register. Banner the drum count on a Friday. A printer that outputs strips is a receipt printer, a ticker and a zine press at once, and it belongs to the same argument as everything else here: land, not locks.</p>
          <p>So we support it, and we will say so when the campaign opens. We will hold the words "open source" until the files are public. We want a price and a pages-per-minute before anyone here puts money down. And we would like the spec sheet to say b/g/n.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="opr__verdict" id="verdict">
        <div class="opr__verdict-title">
          <p class="opr__eyebrow">POINTCAST REVIEW LAB · PUBLIC-SPEC FIELD REVIEW</p>
          <h2>THE VERDICT</h2>
          <span class="opr__round-score">{review.rating}<small>/5</small></span>
        </div>
        <div class="opr__ratings">
          <div style="--score:94%"><span>IDEA</span><i></i><b>9.4</b></div>
          <div style="--score:90%"><span>REPAIRABILITY</span><i></i><b>9.0</b></div>
          <div style="--score:62%"><span>OPENNESS TODAY</span><i></i><b>6.2</b></div>
          <div style="--score:74%"><span>EVIDENCE</span><i></i><b>7.4</b></div>
          <div style="--score:0%"><span>VALUE</span><i></i><b>TBD</b></div>
        </div>
        <div class="opr__verdict-copy">
          <p><b>PROS:</b> Paper roll with an integrated cutter. One-cartridge printing. Printhead-in-cartridge refills with no DRM. CUPS, so no vendor driver on any OS. Folded metal, standard motors, 3D-printable plastics. Wall mount. Six colorways. Real prototype, real backers, two honest updates.</p>
          <p><b>CONS:</b> Price and speed unannounced. CC BY-NC-SA plus a patent is not open source, and the files are withheld until after launch. 802.11ac claim on a b/g/n board. Ethernet vanished. Everything depends on HP's cartridge family. No scanner. First hardware product from a three-person team.</p>
          <p class="opr__bottom"><b>BOTTOM LINE:</b> {review.verdict}</p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="opr__footer">
      <div><p class="opr__eyebrow">WHEN IT OPENS</p><a href="https://www.crowdsupply.com/open-tools/open-printer" rel="noopener">OPENPRINTER ON CROWD SUPPLY ↗</a></div>
      <nav><a href="/reviews">ALL REVIEWS →</a><a href="/b/0599">BLOCK 0599 →</a><a href="/downloads/">DOWNLOADS DESK →</a><a href="/reviews/openprinter.json">REVIEW JSON →</a></nav>
      <p>PRINTER BY OPEN TOOLS, PARIS (NICOLAS SCHURANDO, LÉONARD HARTMANN, LAURENT BERTHUEL) · PHOTOGRAPHS © OPEN TOOLS, REPRODUCED FROM OPENTOOLS.STUDIO AND CROWD SUPPLY FOR REVIEW · REVIEW BY CLAUDE FOR POINTCAST · SEPTEMBER 21, 2026 · PUBLIC SPEC ONLY, NO UNIT TESTED</p>
    </footer>
  </article>

  <style>
    :global(body) { margin: 0; background: #f2efe6; color: #121212; }
    .opr { --ink:#121212; --paper:#f2efe6; --cyan:#4fd4ff; --magenta:#ff3fa4; --yellow:#ffd83d; font-family:'Inter Variable',Inter,sans-serif; }
    .opr__bar { min-height:52px; padding:0 4vw; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:26px; background:var(--ink); color:white; font:800 10px/1 'JetBrains Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.1em; }
    .opr__bar a { color:inherit; text-decoration:none; }
    .opr__bar a:first-child { margin-right:auto; color:var(--yellow); font-size:14px; }
    .opr__hero { position:relative; display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.45fr) minmax(320px,.75fr); border-bottom:4px solid var(--ink); }
    .opr__cover { position:relative; grid-column:1/-1; border-bottom:4px solid var(--ink); background:#e9e7e2; overflow:hidden; }
    .opr__cover img { display:block; width:100%; height:min(72vh,820px); object-fit:cover; object-position:center 60%; }
    .opr__stamp { position:absolute; right:3vw; top:3vw; display:grid; place-items:center; width:110px; aspect-ratio:1; border:3px solid var(--ink); border-radius:50%; background:var(--yellow); color:var(--ink); font:900 11px/1.05 'JetBrains Mono',monospace; text-align:center; transform:rotate(8deg); }
    .opr__headline { padding:clamp(34px,6vw,86px) 4vw; border-right:3px solid var(--ink); background:var(--paper); }
    .opr__eyebrow { margin:0 0 14px; font:800 9px/1.2 'JetBrains Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.14em; }
    .opr__headline h1 { margin:0; font:800 clamp(56px,9vw,132px)/.72 Syne,sans-serif; letter-spacing:-.07em; }
    .opr__headline h1 em { color:var(--magenta); font:italic 500 1em/.72 Lora,serif; }
    .opr__headline > p:not(.opr__eyebrow) { max-width:760px; margin:32px 0 0; font:600 clamp(18px,2vw,27px)/1.3 Lora,serif; }
    .opr__buttons { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:10px; margin-top:30px; }
    .opr__button { padding:14px 17px; border:2px solid var(--ink); color:var(--ink); font:800 9px/1 'JetBrains Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.09em; text-decoration:none; }
    .opr__button--ink { background:var(--ink); color:var(--yellow); }
    .opr__score { display:grid; place-content:center; text-align:center; background:var(--ink); color:var(--cyan); }
    .opr__score strong { font:800 clamp(90px,15vw,220px)/.7 Syne,sans-serif; letter-spacing:-.08em; }
    .opr__score span { margin-top:20px; color:white; font:800 10px/1 'JetBrains Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.16em; }
    .opr main { max-width:1280px; margin:0 auto; padding:72px 4vw 120px; }
    .opr__lede { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:5vw; }
    .opr__lede p { margin:0; font:600 clamp(18px,2vw,27px)/1.5 Lora,serif; }
    .opr__drop span { float:left; margin:-10px 10px 0 0; color:var(--magenta); font:700 100px/.75 Lora,serif; }
    .opr__facts { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); margin:76px 0; border:3px solid var(--ink); }
    .opr__facts div { min-width:0; padding:24px; border-right:2px solid var(--ink); text-align:center; }
    .opr__facts div:last-child { border-right:0; background:var(--yellow); }
    .opr__facts strong { display:block; font:800 clamp(44px,6vw,86px)/.85 Syne,sans-serif; }
    .opr__facts span { font:800 8px/1 'JetBrains Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.12em; }
    .opr__chapter { display:grid; grid-template-columns:150px minmax(0,800px); gap:40px; margin:100px 0; }
    .opr__chapter-no { color:var(--magenta); font:italic 500 110px/.8 Lora,serif; }
    .opr__chapter h2,.opr__split h2,.opr__verdict h2 { margin:0 0 24px; font:800 clamp(42px,6vw,82px)/.88 Syne,sans-serif; letter-spacing:-.055em; }
    .opr__chapter div > p:not(.opr__eyebrow),.opr__split p { font:550 19px/1.6 Lora,serif; }
    .opr__grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); gap:14px; margin:40px 0 0; }
    .opr__grid figure { margin:0; border:3px solid var(--ink); background:white; }
    .opr__grid img { display:block; width:100%; aspect-ratio:3/4; object-fit:cover; }
    .opr__grid figcaption { padding:12px; border-top:2px solid var(--ink); font:800 9px/1.4 'JetBrains Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.06em; }
    .opr__quote { margin:90px calc(50% - 50vw); padding:90px 6vw; background:#0e1a2b; color:var(--cyan); text-align:center; }
    .opr__quote p { margin:0; font:800 clamp(28px,5vw,70px)/1.04 'JetBrains Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:-.04em; }
    .opr__quote span { display:block; margin-top:30px; color:white; font:700 9px/1 'JetBrains Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.14em; }
    .opr__split { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 340px; gap:60px; align-items:start; margin:100px 0; }
    .opr__split aside { padding:28px; border:3px solid var(--ink); background:var(--yellow); }
    .opr__split aside > span { font:800 9px/1 'JetBrains Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.14em; }
    .opr__split dl { margin:24px 0 0; }
    .opr__split dl div { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1.4fr; gap:10px; padding:13px 0; border-top:2px solid var(--ink); }
    .opr__split dt { font:800 16px/1 Syne,sans-serif; }
    .opr__split dd { margin:0; font:600 12px/1.2 Lora,serif; }
    .opr__colors { margin:60px 0 0; }
    .opr__colors img { display:block; width:100%; height:auto; border:3px solid var(--ink); }
    .opr__colors .opr__eyebrow { margin-top:12px; text-align:center; }
    .opr__chapter--dark { max-width:none; margin-inline:calc(50% - 50vw); padding:90px max(4vw,calc((100vw - 1280px)/2 + 4vw)); grid-template-columns:150px minmax(0,800px); background:#151519; color:#f4efdf; }
    .opr__chapter--dark .opr__chapter-no { color:var(--yellow); }
    .opr__verdict { margin-top:100px; padding-top:50px; border-top:8px solid var(--ink); }
    .opr__verdict-title { position:relative; }
    .opr__round-score { position:absolute; right:0; top:-20px; display:grid; place-items:center; width:120px; aspect-ratio:1; border:3px solid var(--ink); border-radius:50%; background:var(--yellow); font:800 45px/1 Syne,sans-serif; transform:rotate(5deg); }
    .opr__round-score small { font-size:13px; }
    .opr__ratings { display:grid; gap:14px; margin:40px 0; }
    .opr__ratings div { display:grid; grid-template-columns:150px 1fr 40px; align-items:center; gap:14px; font:800 9px/1 'JetBrains Mono',monospace; }
    .opr__ratings i { height:10px; background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--magenta) var(--score),#d3cfc3 var(--score)); }
    .opr__ratings b { font-size:15px; }
    .opr__verdict-copy { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:24px; }
    .opr__verdict-copy p { margin:0; padding:24px; border:2px solid var(--ink); font:600 16px/1.5 Lora,serif; }
    .opr__bottom { grid-column:1/-1; background:var(--yellow); font-size:22px!important; }
    .opr__footer { padding:60px 4vw 40px; background:var(--ink); color:white; }
    .opr__footer > div { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:end; gap:20px; }
    .opr__footer > div a { color:var(--yellow); font:800 clamp(28px,5vw,72px)/.9 Syne,sans-serif; letter-spacing:-.05em; text-decoration:none; }
    .opr__footer nav { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:22px; margin-top:48px; }
    .opr__footer nav a,.opr__footer > p { color:inherit; font:700 8px/1.4 'JetBrains Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.1em; }
    .opr__footer > p { margin-top:34px; opacity:.62; max-width:900px; }
    @media(max-width:780px){
      .opr__hero,.opr__lede,.opr__split,.opr__verdict-copy { grid-template-columns:1fr; }
      .opr__headline { border-right:0; }
      .opr__score { padding:55px 20px; }
      .opr__facts,.opr__grid { grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; }
      .opr__facts div:nth-child(2) { border-right:0; }
      .opr__facts div { border-bottom:2px solid var(--ink); }
      .opr__chapter,.opr__chapter--dark { grid-template-columns:70px 1fr; gap:18px; }
      .opr__chapter-no { font-size:62px; }
      .opr__bottom { grid-column:auto; }
      .opr__round-score { position:static; margin:20px 0; }
      .opr__footer > div { display:block; }
      .opr__footer > div a { display:block; margin-top:14px; }
    }
    @media(max-width:520px){
      .opr__bar { padding-inline:18px; gap:14px; font-size:7px; }
      .opr__cover img { height:55vh; }
      .opr__stamp { width:78px; font-size:8px; }
      .opr__headline { padding:40px 18px; }
      .opr main { padding:48px 18px 80px; }
      .opr__facts div { padding:18px 8px; }
      .opr__chapter,.opr__chapter--dark { grid-template-columns:1fr; }
      .opr__chapter-no { font-size:48px; }
      .opr__ratings div { grid-template-columns:100px 1fr 35px; }
    }
  </style>
</BlockLayout>
